[32m+[m[32m## Time and Date Handling[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll timestamps stored in the SQLite database must use UTC Unix time in milliseconds.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRules:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Store timestamps in SQLite as `INTEGER`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Store only UTC timestamps.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Never store local time in the database.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use `DateTimeOffset` throughout the application.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Convert between Unix time and `DateTimeOffset` only within the persistence layer.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Convert to the user's local time only when displaying dates in the user interface.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis keeps storage implementation details isolated from the rest of the application and avoids timezone and daylight saving issues.[m
